    "explanation": "Decision: NO_ACTION. The 5.00 SGD already refunded to the rider stays with her and is not recovered for the driver; both amount fields are null, and no referral arises. Because the driver filed, the question is whether his claim against the present state is supported, and it is not.\n\nEverything turns on one fact: whether the driver cancelled after the free wait. Under POL-NS-21 the 300 s free wait on this on-demand trip runs from the driver's arrival, and the auto-arrival event and the corroborated GPS trace fix that at 10:37:25 (EV-TRIP-06054; EV-GPS-06054, both weight 1.0, COMPLETE), so the wait ended at 10:42:25. The cancellation was logged at 10:42:10 — 285 s after arrival, 15 s short (trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait.cancelled_after_free_wait = false). POL-NS-22 authorises the 5.00 SGD fee and its transfer to the driver as compensation only 'when the driver cancels after the free wait'. That condition was not met, so no fee was chargeable and none is owed to the driver. The driver's point that POL-NS-21 attaches no separate monetary penalty to a premature cancellation is right but does not help him: this is not a penalty on the driver, it is the fee's own precondition, and the precondition failed. The rider's account ('less than 5 minutes') is what the record bears out.\n\nThe driver's remaining points do not change this. The contact obligation in POL-NS-23 was met — two in-app messages (10:37:50 and 10:40:20) and one unanswered in-app call (10:41:05), all before the 10:42:10 cancellation, as both sides accept — so POL-NS-23 does not void the fee; equally it does not revive it. POL-NS-24 is not engaged: the driver did arrive (a GPS fix 3.99 m from the pickup, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius), so there is no driver no-show and no 5.00 SGD goodwill credit referral. The 11:17:10 reversal was recorded as interim, but POL-GEN-03 makes NO_ACTION the outcome where the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands, and