    "explanation": "The driver filed to undo the 5.00 SGD refund already issued to the rider and recovered from him. On the record, that refund is correct and the driver's claim fails, so the present state stands (NO_ACTION) and no money moves in either direction.\n\nWhy the fee cannot stand: POL-NS-21 sets a free wait of 300 s (5 minutes) which, on this on-demand trip, runs from the driver's arrival. The platform's arrival event, corroborated by the driver-device GPS trace (nearest fix 3.99 m from the pickup, inside the 50 m STANDARD radius, accuracy 5 m), puts the driver at the pickup at 10:37:25, so the free wait ended at 10:42:25 (the platform's own wait timer started at 10:37:30 and would have ended at 10:42:30). The driver cancelled at 10:42:10, 285 s after arrival — 15 s short on either reading, and trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait.cancelled_after_free_wait is false. POL-NS-22 authorises the 5.00 SGD no-show fee only 'when the driver cancels after the free wait'; that condition is not met, so the fee was not authorised. The 5.00 SGD was reversed at 11:17:10 (fare ledger payment_status REFUNDED, refund_issued_sgd 5.00) and the rider keeps it.\n\nThe driver's arguments, and what they meet: the POL-NS-23 contact obligation was satisfied — two in-app messages (MSG-06054-001 at 10:37:50, MSG-06054-002 at 10:40:20) and one in-app call (10:41:05, unanswered, 18 s) all before the 10:42:10 cancellation — so no FULL_REFUND arises on that clause; I accept that, and it does not cure the timing. The arrival was corroborated and the driver waited stationary at the pickup throughout the window (22 fixes, 30 s spacing, 100% coverage, no gap over 30 s), so POL-NS-24's premise (a driver who never arrived) is absent and no 5.00 SGD goodwill credit is owed. The fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD policy figure (fee_matches_policy = true), so POL-NS-22's fee-amount check produces no referral. I reject the argument that POL-NS-21 carries no monetary consequence of its own: POL-NS-